[l_braz_por.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
O palácio imperial

[l_braz_por.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
O Palácio Imperial de Tóquio é a residência principal do Imperador, e assim tem sido desde a Restauração Meiji e a queda do último xogunato. É um símbolo de orgulho e reverência para o povo japonês, que os inspira a trabalhar com dedicação.

[l_braz_por.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_english.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
The Imperial Palace

[l_english.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
The Tokyo Imperial Palace is the main residence of the Emperor, and has been so since the Meiji Restoration and the ousting of the last Shogunate. It is a symbol of pride and reverence for the Japanese people, and inspires them to work hard.

[l_english.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_french.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
Le palais impérial

[l_french.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
Le palais impérial de Tokyo est la résidence principale de l'empereur depuis la restauration de Meiji et la fin du dernier shogunat. Aux yeux du peuple japonais, c'est aussi un symbole de fierté et de dévotion qui lui apporte l'inspiration nécessaire pour travailler dur.

[l_french.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_german.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
Kaiserlicher Palast

[l_german.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
Der Kaiserpalast von Tokio ist die Hauptresidenz des Kaisers und das seit der Meiji-Restauration und der Abschaffung des letzten Schogunats. Er ist dem japanischen Volk ein Symbol des Stolzes und der Verehrung und inspiriert es, hart zu arbeiten.

[l_german.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_japanese.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
皇居

[l_japanese.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
皇居は明治維新で最後の幕府より明け渡されて以来続く、天皇陛下の主な居所である。日本人にとって皇居は誇りと敬意の象徴であり、勤勉の励みとなっている。

[l_japanese.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_korean.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
황궁

[l_korean.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
도쿄 황궁은 천황의 주요 거처로서, 메이지 유신과 마지막 쇼군의 사임 이후 지금까지 그 자리를 지켜왔습니다. 일본 국민의 자부심과 경외심의 상징이자, 그들이 열심히 일하도록 영감을 주는 곳입니다.

[l_korean.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_polish.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
Pałac cesarski

[l_polish.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
Pałac cesarski w Tokio jest główną rezydencją cesarza od czasu restauracji Meiji i obalenia ostatniego szogunatu. Jest symbolem dumy i szacunku dla Japończyków oraz inspiruje ich do ciężkiej pracy.

[l_polish.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_russian.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
Императорский дворец

[l_russian.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
Со времен Реставрации Мэйдзи и свержения последнего сёгуна императорский дворец в Токио был главной резиденцией императора. Это символ гордости и почтительности японского народа, вдохновляющий его на усердный труд.

[l_russian.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_simp_chinese.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
皇居

[l_simp_chinese.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
东京皇居是自明治维新最后一任幕府被推翻以来天皇的主要居所，它是日本人民自豪与崇敬的象征，激励着他们努力工作。

[l_simp_chinese.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

[l_spanish.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace]
Palacio imperial

[l_spanish.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_desc]
El Palacio Imperial de Tokio es la residencia principal del emperador desde que se derrocara al último shogunato en tiempos de la Restauración Meiji. Para el pueblo japonés es un símbolo de orgullo y reverencia, un aliciente que lo inspira a trabajar con total dedicación.

[l_spanish.landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace_plural]
$landmark_tokyo_imperial_palace$

